{
  "raw": {
    "https://wittenberg.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205693": {
      "title": "Director of Assessment and Licensure",
      "description": "Wittenberg University\nJob Posting: Director of Assessment and Licensure Wittenberg University \n\tJob Posting: Director of Assessment and Licensure Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Director of Assessment and Licensure Category: Administrative Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Education Locations: Springfield, OH Posted: Oct 12, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: 1-82054-501001 Position ID: 205693 Share About Wittenberg University: In surveying the grounds of what is now Wittenberg University, the Rev. Ezra Keller, the college's first president and founder, remarked: \"This is a lovely spot for a literary institution,\" one that will attract hundreds of students \"to drink at the pure fountains of knowledge, and then go forth into the world to do good.\" Today, that lovely spot now encompasses more than 100 acres of rolling hills and lush hollows across southwestern Ohio with architecturally distinct structures that embrace Wittenberg's past and provide a beautiful backdrop to the teaching excellence and faith-based learning environment that has defined the liberal arts University since its founding in 1845. Nationally recognized for accessible professors, best classroom experience, service excellence, and a superior athletics tradition, Wittenberg is home to 1,700 students, 60 majors, minors and special programs, a Graduate School for Professional Studies, and 25 varsity sports. Job Description: The Department of Education in the School of Health, Education, and Sport Studies at Wittenberg University is seeking a Director of Assessment and Licensure. This is a full-time, 10-month administrative staff position. Working under the direction of the Dean and Department Chairperson, this position oversees and directs the assessment system for the University's undergraduate teacher licensure programs and graduate level principal and endorsement programs. This position will lead and coordinate assessment reporting (inclusive of the Council for the Accreditation of Educator Preparation [CAEP], the USDOE, and the state of Ohio) through the use and management of databases and electronic assessment systems. Additionally, this position will work with faculty to establish and maintain key assessments for the entire unit and individual licensure programs. This position will develop data summaries and recommendations related to the Education programs' key assessments, monitor changes in state and national policy, and report the findings and recommendations to the Dean, the Department Chair and the Director of Graduate Studies. Additionally, this position will recommend to the Ohio Department of Education, those candidates who have completed licensure and endorsement requirements based on Wittenberg's approved programs. This position will also teach undergraduate and/or graduate level teacher Education courses, based on their area of expertise and as the assessment cycle allows. This position requires some travel within the state of Ohio and to national meetings. Essential functions include, but are not limited to: -Lead and coordinate assessment reporting (inclusive of CAEP, SPA, Title II, -AACTE, PEDS, and State of Ohio) through the use and management of databases or electronic assessment systems - Be the primary liaison to the Ohio Department of Education and the Ohio -Department of Higher Education to monitor changes to licensure requirements and licensure testing expectations - Recommend to the Ohio Department of Education those candidates who have completed licensure and endorsement requirements based on Wittenberg's approved programs - Create and maintain the unit and programs' assessment systems necessary to adequately evaluate program outcomes - Coordinate the writing and submission of the accreditation, SPA, state, and national reports to be filed at relevant deadlines throughout the accreditation cycle - Act as system administrator for electronic data collection systems (Via by Watermark) and edTPA/Pearson coordinator - Review all completers' programs of study and recommend to the Ohio Department of Education those candidates who have completed licensure/endorsement requirements - Assist with required background check and state requirements for field, practica, and licensure. - Attend trainings and conferences that pertain to accreditation, teacher education programs and teacher licensing at both the state and national level - Conduct training/orientations for teacher candidates to assure correct licensure exams and licensure applications are completed - Teach up to 16 credit hours each academic year - Demonstrate support for community and belonging, as well as participate in maintaining a respectful, positive work environment - Perform other relevant duties as assigned, such as special projects, programs, and developmental activities Requirements: -Bachelor's degree or Master's degree in Education -1-3 years of experience in higher education or related areas - Knowledge and experience working with teacher accreditation and assessment processes - Knowledge and experience working with electronic data collection systems · Must be able to successfully pass a criminal background check as required Preferred Qualifications include - PhD or EdD in Education - Previous Teaching Experience in P-12 Additional Information: Wittenberg is committed to attracting and retaining highly qualified individuals who collectively reflect the diversity of our student body and society at-large.  Please see our notice of nondiscrimination housed on our website. The successful candidate will demonstrate support for diversity, equity and inclusiveness as well as participate in maintaining a respectful, positive work environment. Application Instructions: Review of applications will begin immediately, and the position will remain open until filled. The anticipated start date for this role is tentatively January 2027. Questions regarding the position should be directed to John Thistlethwaite, Dean of the School of Health, Education and Sports Studies, Wittenberg University, thistlethwaitej@wittenberg.edu. To apply, please set-up an account in our online recruiting system and upload the following documents in MS Word or Adobe Acrobat format. 1. Resume 2. Cover letter 3. Name, address, and phone number of three professional references. If you are a person with a disability and require assistance with the application process, please contact Wittenberg's Human Resources Department at 937.327.7517. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Wittenberg University Wittenberg Ave, Springfield, OH 45501-0720"
    },
    "https://wittenberg.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205230": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach, Women's Basketball",
      "description": "Wittenberg University\nJob Posting: Assistant Coach, Women's Basketball Wittenberg University \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Coach, Women's Basketball Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Coach, Women's Basketball Category: Administrative Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Athletics Locations: Springfield, OH Posted: Sep 25, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: 1-90003-50101 Position ID: 205230 Share About Wittenberg University: In surveying the grounds of what is now Wittenberg University, the Rev. Ezra Keller, the college's first president and founder, remarked: \"This is a lovely spot for a literary institution.\" Today, that lovely spot encompasses more than 100 acres of rolling hills and hollows in southwestern Ohio, with architecturally distinctive structures that embrace Wittenberg's past and provide a beautiful backdrop to the teaching excellence and Lutheran-affiliated learning environment that has defined Wittenberg University since its founding in 1845. Nationally recognized for accessible professors, engaging classroom experiences, service opportunities, and valued athletics traditions, Wittenberg is home to 1,500 students, 60 majors, minors and special programs, three graduate programs, and 25 varsity sports. Wittenberg University is committed to providing a comprehensive and competitive employee benefits package that attracts and retains talent to further the university's mission and contributes to the personal and financial well-being of employees and their families.  From healthcare to our tuition benefit to vacation and holidays, our goal is to help our employees enjoy happy and healthy lifestyles, while maintaining a good work-life balance. Click here to learn more about Wittenberg's employee benefits. Job Description: Wittenberg University is seeking applications for an Assistant Coach for the Women's Basketball program. This individual will assist the head coach in leading all aspects of an NCAA Division III Women's Basketball program.  This is a full-time, 12-month, exempt-level position reporting to the Head Women's Basketball Coach. Essential functions include, but are not limited to: Assist the head coach with practice and game-day preparation and execution. Evaluate, recruit, and graduate student-athletes. Provide service to the Institution as assigned by Director of Athletics & Recreation, reporting to the Assistant Athletic Director for Facilities & Events. Maintain and ensure student-athlete academic integrity. Interact effectively and appropriately with student-athletes, parents, alumni, faculty, peers, community members, and administrators. Conduct student-worker hiring, training, and supervision. Adhere to NCAA, conference, departmental, and university policies, procedures, and expectations. Perform other relevant duties as assigned such as special projects, programs, developmental activities, etc. Requirements: For this position, we require that candidates have: Bachelor's degree Minimum 1-3 years of previous collegiate coaching or playing experience with the post position. Candidates must possess excellent organizational and communication skills, be able to interact effectively and appropriately with student-athletes, parents, alumni, faculty, peers, community members, and administrators. Knowledge in the following areas is preferred:  Microsoft Office, athletic video and performance review software (i.e. Hudl, Synergy), social media platforms, and recruiting software (i.e. Frontrush). Travel is required as well as some evening, night, and weekend work. A valid driver's license is required; must meet required insurance qualifications found in Wittenberg Motor Pool policies and procedures. If license is from out of state, successful candidate will need to obtain a valid Ohio driver's license within 30 days of hire date. Additional Information: Wittenberg is committed to attracting and retaining highly qualified individuals who collectively reflect the diversity of our student body and society at-large.  Please see our notice of nondiscrimination housed on our website. Wittenberg University is committed to preventing and addressing sexual misconduct in our campus community. Click here to view our Title IX policies. The successful candidate will demonstrate support for diversity, equity and inclusiveness as well as participate in maintaining a respectful, positive work environment. Employment at Wittenberg University is contingent upon satisfactory completion of applicable background checks including but not limited to: criminal records, educational verifications, driving records (when job-related), and/or credit history (when job related). Application Instructions: Review of applications will begin immediately and the position will remain open until filled. To apply, please set-up an account in our online recruiting system and upload the following documents in MS Word or Adobe Acrobat format. Resume Cover letter Name, address, and phone number of three professional references. Applicants who require accommodation during any stage of the hiring process should contact the Office of Human Resources at (937) 327-7517 or email hure-mail@wittenberg.edu. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Wittenberg University Wittenberg Ave, Springfield, OH 45501-0720"
    },
    "https://wittenberg.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204844": {
      "title": "Assistant Men's Basketball Coach",
      "description": "Wittenberg University\nJob Posting: Assistant Men's Basketball Coach Wittenberg University \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Men's Basketball Coach Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Men's Basketball Coach Category: Administrative Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Athletics Locations: Springfield, OH Posted: Sep 16, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: 1-90032-50101 Position ID: 204844 Share About Wittenberg University: In surveying the grounds of what is now Wittenberg University, the Rev. Ezra Keller, the college's first president and founder, remarked: \"This is a lovely spot for a literary institution.\" Today, that lovely spot encompasses more than 100 acres of rolling hills and hollows in southwestern Ohio, with architecturally distinctive structures that embrace Wittenberg's past and provide a beautiful backdrop to the teaching excellence and Lutheran-affiliated learning environment that has defined Wittenberg University since its founding in 1845. Nationally recognized for accessible professors, engaging classroom experiences, service opportunities, and valued athletics traditions, Wittenberg is home to 1,500 students, 60 majors, minors and special programs, three graduate programs, and 25 varsity sports. Wittenberg University is committed to providing a comprehensive and competitive employee benefits package that attracts and retains talent to further the university's mission and contributes to the personal and financial well-being of employees and their families.  From healthcare to our tuition benefit to vacation and holidays, our goal is to help our employees enjoy happy and healthy lifestyles, while maintaining a good work-life balance. Click here to learn more about Wittenberg's employee benefits. Job Description: Wittenberg University is accepting applications for a full-time Assistant Men's Basketball Coach. The Assistant Coach assists the Head Coach with the daily operation of the men's basketball program in the NCAA Division III and the recruitment of student-athletes. This is a full-time, 12-month, exempt-level position. Essential functions include, but are not limited to: Coaching Assist the Head Coach with daily practice planning, game decisions, and player feedback and evaluation. Perform video analysis and scouting of opponents. Assist and mentor student athletes with academic progress, course selection, campus involvement and social/community outreach, and other issues related to the college experience. Recruiting Recruit quality student-athletes both on campus and at various recruiting events throughout the year. Manage recruiting databases. Schedule recruit visits. Attend recruiting events and evaluate prospective student-athletes. Administrative Assist the Head Coach with coordinating and managing game day operations and administrative tasks. Plan team travel and meals. Participate in department meetings. Provide service to the Institution as assigned by the Director of Athletics & Recreation or the Head Coach. Adhere to NCAA, conference, departmental, and university policies, procedures, and expectations. Perform other relevant duties as assigned such as special projects, programs, developmental activities, etc. Requirements: Bachelor's degree required 1-3 years of previous collegiate coaching or playing experience with the post position. Candidates must possess excellent organizational and communication skills, be able to interact effectively and appropriately with student-athletes, parents, alumni, faculty, peers, community members, and administrators. Knowledge in the following areas is preferred:  Microsoft Office, athletic video and performance review software (i.e. Hudl, Synergy), social media platforms, and recruiting software (i.e. Frontrush). CPR and First Aid certification, or willingness to obtain CPR and First Aid certification required. Ability to remain stationary for several hours during games and practices routinely transport equipment and supplies weighing up to 50 pounds (with assistance), and ability to use technology such as computer, tablet, and/or phone required. Travel is required as well as some evening, night, and weekend work. A valid driver's license is required; must meet required insurance qualifications found in Wittenberg Motor Pool policies and procedures. If license is from out of state, successful candidate will need to obtain a valid Ohio driver's license within 30 days of hire date. Additional Information: Wittenberg is committed to attracting and retaining highly qualified individuals who collectively reflect the diversity of our student body and society at-large.  Please see our notice of nondiscrimination housed on our website. Wittenberg University is committed to preventing and addressing sexual misconduct in our campus community. Click here to view our Title IX policies. The successful candidate will demonstrate support for diversity, equity and inclusiveness as well as participate in maintaining a respectful, positive work environment. Employment at Wittenberg University is contingent upon satisfactory completion of applicable background checks including but not limited to: criminal records, educational verifications, driving records (when job-related), and/or credit history (when job related). Application Instructions: Review of applications will begin immediately and the position will remain open until filled. To apply, please set-up an account in our online recruiting system and upload the following documents in MS Word or Adobe Acrobat format. Resume Cover letter Name, address, and phone number of three professional references. Applicants who require accommodation during any stage of the hiring process should contact the Office of Human Resources at (937) 327-7517 or email hure-mail@wittenberg.edu. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Wittenberg University Wittenberg Ave, Springfield, OH 45501-0720"
