    "https://wittenberg.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204082": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Housing Operations",
      "description": "Wittenberg University\nJob Posting: Associate Director of Housing Operations Wittenberg University \n\tJob Posting: Associate Director of Housing Operations Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Associate Director of Housing Operations Category: Administrative Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Residence Life Locations: Springfield, OH Posted: Aug 25, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: 1-84011-50101 Position ID: 204082 Share About Wittenberg University: In surveying the grounds of what is now Wittenberg University, the Rev. Ezra Keller, the college's first president and founder, remarked: \"This is a lovely spot for a literary institution.\" Today, that lovely spot encompasses more than 100 acres of rolling hills and hollows in southwestern Ohio, with architecturally distinctive structures that embrace Wittenberg's past and provide a beautiful backdrop to the teaching excellence and Lutheran-affiliated learning environment that has defined Wittenberg University since its founding in 1845. Nationally recognized for accessible professors, engaging classroom experiences, service opportunities, and valued athletics traditions, Wittenberg is home to 1,500 students, 60 majors, minors and special programs, three graduate programs, and 25 varsity sports. Wittenberg University is committed to providing a comprehensive and competitive employee benefits package that attracts and retains talent to further the university's mission and contributes to the personal and financial well-being of employees and their families.  From healthcare to our tuition benefit to vacation and holidays, our goal is to help our employees enjoy happy and healthy lifestyles, while maintaining a good work-life balance. Click here to learn more about Wittenberg's employee benefits. Job Description: The Associate Director of Housing and Operations supports the mission of the University by managing the University's housing operations program under the leadership of the Associate Dean of Students and Director of Residence Life and in collaboration with other professional staff. The position manages housing operations for Wittenberg's fully residential campus. Professional staff members and student leaders work together to cultivate safe and inclusive living communities. This is a twelve-month, exempt-level position that includes evening and weekend responsibilities. Essential functions include, but are not limited to: HOUSING & OPERATIONS RESPONSIBILITIES: Coordinate campus housing operations program for 1,500 beds located in traditional residence halls (six) and over 100 student rental properties, including 2 apartment buildings. Oversee the development and implementation of campus housing assignment processes and occupancy management functions, including, but not limited to, housing selection, first-year housing assignments, room changes, and damage billing. Prepare and maintain occupancy records and procedures pertaining to campus housing, including but not limited to designations, rates, maintenance records, occupancy reports, requests and approvals, changes, etc. Ensure meal plan and housing software, related databases, and other means of maintaining accurate student and facility records are up to date and accurate. Collaborate with conferencing services staff to manage office housing processes, including, but not limited to, move-in/move-out, early arrivals, and break, transition, and summer housing. Collaborate with Facilities and Housekeeping to manage residential building repairs and custodial needs. Communicate relevant information with other campus offices such as Facilities, Housekeeping, Scheduling & Events, Police, Conduct, Student Accounts, and approved contractors and vendors. Complete monthly walk-throughs of residential spaces with Residential Life Area Coordinators (ACs). Assist with the coordination and support of housing operations during campus emergencies. Serve as a member of the Residential Life team; develop and maintain mutually supportive and collaborative working relationships with conferencing services staff, ACs, resident advisors, and other staff. Collaborate with Campus Safety to develop and implement health, safety, and emergency response materials and training opportunities for students, Community Advisors, Resident Advisors and professional staff members. Partner with the Office of Student Accessibility Services to identify housing assignments for students with approved ADA housing accommodations and/or Emotional Support Animals (ESAs); ensure students with approved ESAs are aware of and follow ESA policies. Collaborate with campus partners to coordinate housing needs for New Student Move-In, Commencement, and Summer Conferences. Ensure compliance with relevant codes, laws, and ordinances related to campus housing. OTHER RESPONSIBILITIES: Participate in the professional, on-call duty rotation for the Division of Student Development, providing 24-hour crisis intervention, on-site emergency response, and support to other campus partners. Campus housing will be provided or you can live within 10 minutes of campus. Assist in the implementation and enforcement of college policies and expectations.  Assist in development and interpretation of policies and procedures relating to campus housing. Develop and maintain courteous and effective working relationships with student development colleagues, faculty, and campus partners. Continuously identify and address the developmental needs of students through educational interactions, crisis response protocols, and mediations; advise and provide general support to students. Ensure excellent customer service for students, families, alumni, and campus guests. Develop meaningful connections with students, staff and faculty by being available and visible on campus. Assist with special projects and other duties as needed. Requirements: A Master's degree in college student affairs, higher education administration, or other related area is required. 3 - 5 years of experience with housing and residence life operations is required. Competency and experience with Microsoft Excel, Publisher, Outlook, and PowerPoint is necessary. Familiarity with property management, landlord tenant laws, group housing in a higher education environment are preferred. Familiarity with Adirondack, CBORD, Datatel Ellucian Colleague, and JotForm is helpful. Ability to communicate effectively. Ability to navigate through university facilities including but not limited to stairs, elevators, areas without air conditioning, uneven surfaces, and across campus terrain. Ability to transport items and equipment weighing up to 50 pounds (with assistance). Ability to utilize computer, office phone, cell phone, and tablet as needed. While this position primarily operates during normal business hours, there are some evening and weekend hours expected as needed. This position requires ability to work with a variety of constituents, solve problems quickly and professionally, anticipate needs, and communicate proactively. An understanding of how to prioritize competing demands and timelines is necessary. A valid driver's license is required; must meet required insurance qualifications found in Wittenberg Motor Pool policies and procedures. If license is from out of state, successful candidate will need to obtain a valid Ohio driver's license within 30 days of hire date. Additional Information: Wittenberg is committed to attracting and retaining highly qualified individuals who collectively reflect the diversity of our student body and society at-large.  Please see our notice of nondiscrimination housed on our website. Wittenberg University is committed to preventing and addressing sexual misconduct in our campus community. Click here to view our Title IX policies . The successful candidate will demonstrate support for diversity, equity and inclusiveness as well as participate in maintaining a respectful, positive work environment. Employment at Wittenberg University is contingent upon satisfactory completion of applicable background checks including but not limited to: criminal records, educational verifications, driving records (when job-related), and/or credit history (when job related). Application Instructions: Review of applications will begin immediately and the position will remain open until filled. To apply, please set-up an account in our online recruiting system and upload the following documents in MS Word or Adobe Acrobat format. 1. Resume 2. Cover letter 3. Name, address, and phone number of three professional references. Applicants who require accommodation during any stage of the hiring process should contact the Office of Human Resources at (937) 327-7517 or email hure-mail@wittenberg.edu. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Wittenberg University Wittenberg Ave, Springfield, OH 45501-0720"
    },
    "https://wittenberg.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203760": {
      "title": "Director, Campus Scheduling and Event Services",
      "description": "Wittenberg University\nJob Posting: Director, Campus Scheduling and Event Services Wittenberg University \n\tJob Posting: Director, Campus Scheduling and Event Services Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Director, Campus Scheduling and Event Services Category: Administrative Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Administration Locations: Springfield, OH Posted: Aug 16, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: 1-84016-50101 Position ID: 203760 Share About Wittenberg University: In surveying the grounds of what is now Wittenberg University, the Rev. Ezra Keller, the college's first president and founder, remarked: \"This is a lovely spot for a literary institution.\" Today, that lovely spot encompasses more than 100 acres of rolling hills and hollows in southwestern Ohio, with architecturally distinctive structures that embrace Wittenberg's past and provide a beautiful backdrop to the teaching excellence and Lutheran-affiliated learning environment that has defined Wittenberg University since its founding in 1845. Nationally recognized for accessible professors, engaging classroom experiences, service opportunities, and valued athletics traditions, Wittenberg is home to 1,500 students, 60 majors, minors and special programs, three graduate programs, and 25 varsity sports. Wittenberg University is committed to providing a comprehensive and competitive employee benefits package that attracts and retains talent to further the university's mission and contributes to the personal and financial well-being of employees and their families.  From healthcare to our tuition benefit to vacation and holidays, our goal is to help our employees enjoy happy and healthy lifestyles, while maintaining a good work-life balance. Click here to learn more about Wittenberg's employee benefits. Job Description: Wittenberg University is accepting applications for the position of Director, Campus Scheduling & Event Services. The position will provide administrative and logistical support to a variety of clients across the Wittenberg community through management and leadership of the University scheduling system.  They will ensure the successful execution of different types of university events, workshops, meetings, classes, and facility spaces.  This position is responsible for ensuring that the multitude of details and mechanics required to produce events that are successful through high-quality coordination and management. This is a full-time, exempt-level position reporting to the Vice President of Finance and Administration. Essential functions include but are not limited to: Serve as primary University administrator for 25Live by Collegenet, scheduling and approving space for meetings and events, effectively using scheduling software to include allowance for set up, staffing and tear down by support services. Identify, train, and assign responsibilities to superuser administrators across campus, monitor the operation of 25Live, and identify and recommend policy updates and campus wide operation needs. Liaise as needed with Information Technology and Collegenet (software vendor) to ensure 25Live system has the latest software updates and is utilized by campus users in the most effective way.  Contact as necessary to ensure efficient and user-friendly operation. Act as a liaison when scheduling space in buildings on campus.  Work with campus partners to ensure efficient policy implementation, scheduling operations, and set up processes. Advise clients and facilitate event planning meetings as needed; prepare set-up diagrams, coordinate reservations and utilize the current scheduling systems. Assist with the enforcement of facility policies and procedures along with customer service initiatives. Create and manage a university event calendar ensuring effective communication and awareness of campus events. Support event managers for other University-wide events or initiatives as necessary. Perform other relevant duties as assigned such as special projects, programs, developmental activities, etc. Requirements: Requirements include: A bachelor's degree or equivalent experience required. A Master's degree in higher education/student affairs is preferred. One to three years experience with event planning and marketing to a wide variety of constituents is required. Experience in a student union or educational setting is preferred. Experience as supervisor/manager. Experience using 25Live or other enterprise scheduling software is preferred. Excellent customer service, time management, and communication skills. Ability to work with a variety of constituents, solve problems quickly and professionally, anticipate needs, and communicate proactively. Competency and experience using Microsoft Office software, specifically proficient in the use of Excel, Publisher, Outlook, and PowerPoint with the ability and desire to learn additional software applications as necessary. Night and weekend work may be required depending on campus events and needs. Ability to lift up to 50 lbs. with assistance. A valid driver's license is required; must meet required insurance qualifications found in Wittenberg Motor Pool policies and procedures. Additional Information: Wittenberg is committed to attracting and retaining highly qualified individuals who collectively reflect the diversity of our student body and society at-large.  Please see our notice of nondiscrimination housed on our website. Wittenberg University is committed to preventing and addressing sexual misconduct in our campus community. Click here to view our Title IX policies . The successful candidate will demonstrate support for diversity, equity and inclusiveness as well as participate in maintaining a respectful, positive work environment. Employment at Wittenberg University is contingent upon satisfactory completion of applicable background checks including but not limited to: criminal records, educational verifications, driving records (when job-related), and/or credit history (when job related). Application Instructions: Review of applications will begin immediately and the position will remain open until filled. To apply, please set-up an account in our online recruiting system and upload the following documents in MS Word or Adobe Acrobat format. Resume Cover letter Name, address, and phone number of three professional references. Applicants who require accommodation during any stage of the hiring process should contact the Office of Human Resources at (937) 327-7517 or email hure-mail@wittenberg.edu. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Wittenberg University Wittenberg Ave, Springfield, OH 45501-0720"
    },
    "https://wittenberg.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203759": {
      "title": "Associate Director External Partnerships, Lead Personal & Professional Development Coach",
      "description": "Wittenberg University\nJob Posting: Associate Director External Partnerships, Lead Personal & Professional Development Coach Wittenberg University \n\tJob Posting: Associate Director External Partnerships, Lead Personal & Professional Development Coach Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Associate Director External Partnerships, Lead Personal & Professional Development Coach Category: Administrative Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Student Engagement Locations: Springfield, OH Posted: Aug 15, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: 1-84016-50101 Position ID: 203759 Share About Wittenberg University: In surveying the grounds of what is now Wittenberg University, the Rev. Ezra Keller, the college's first president and founder, remarked: \"This is a lovely spot for a literary institution.\" Today, that lovely spot encompasses more than 100 acres of rolling hills and hollows in southwestern Ohio, with architecturally distinctive structures that embrace Wittenberg's past and provide a beautiful backdrop to the teaching excellence and Lutheran-affiliated learning environment that has defined Wittenberg University since its founding in 1845. Nationally recognized for accessible professors, engaging classroom experiences, service opportunities, and valued athletics traditions, Wittenberg is home to 1,200 students, 30 majors, 3 graduate programs, a wealth of pre-professional and cooperative programs, and 25 varsity sports. Wittenberg University is committed to providing a comprehensive and competitive employee benefits package that attracts and retains talent to further the university's mission and contributes to the personal and financial well-being of employees and their families.  From healthcare to our tuition benefit to vacation and holidays, our goal is to help our employees enjoy happy and healthy lifestyles, while maintaining a good work-life balance. Click here to learn more about Wittenberg's employee benefits. Job Description: The Associate Director of External Partnerships & Lead Personal and Professional Development Coach combines leadership in external partnerships with hands-on coaching responsibilities to support the personal and professional growth of students. The Associate Director will use insights from student coaching to inform partnership development (e.g., aligning the right partners with student needs), bring partnership opportunities into coaching practice (e.g., connecting clients with external resources or networks), and will serve as a bridge between internal coaching teams and external stakeholders, ensuring alignment between programs and external collaborations. The Wittenberg Center for Personal and Professional Development (CPPD) is designed to help students grow both personally and professionally. \"Rooted and Open\" calls ELCA universities, rooted in Lutheran theology, to help students explore larger questions about their purpose and calling in life. The center offers structured and informal opportunities for self-reflection, discernment, conversations about vocation and calling, goal setting, and skill-building. This will include individual and group coaching sessions, workshops, guest speakers, identity-building activities, and professional experiential learning opportunities. Responsible for building and maintaining relationships with external organizations, employers, graduate school admissions teams, and stakeholders including, but not limited to: Identifying and securing partnerships that align with the Center's mission and goals. Negotiating and managing agreements, contracts, and collaboration frameworks. Representing the Center in meetings, events, and outreach programs. Leveraging partnerships to expand resources, programs, and opportunities for students. Tracking and reporting on the impact of these partnerships Conducting 1:1 coaching sessions to help students identify strengths, set goals, and develop action plans. Facilitating group workshops, seminars, and leadership programs to build skills in communication, collaboration, self-reflection, and career navigation. Monitoring individual student progress, providing feedback, and adjusting strategies to meet evolving needs. Acting as a mentor and accountability partner, encouraging students to step outside their comfort zones and take actionable steps toward interests, goals, and plans. Maintaining confidentiality and professionalism in all coaching interactions. Demonstrate support for community and belonging, as well as participate in maintaining a respectful, positive work environment Requirements: Education: Bachelor's degree in counseling, business or related area of study. Experience: 3-5 years of relevant work experience in career advising, career counseling, life coaching, leadership coaching, mentoring or related field Technical Skills: Microsoft Office Must be able to demonstrate the ability to take initiative. Demonstrated experience building relationships with key constituents. Demonstrated success on a team. Strong written, public speaking, and interpersonal communication skills. Demonstrated ability to give polished and professional presentations. Demonstrated success delivering personal and professional development advice. Experience advising on resumes, interviewing and job search strategies. Ability to have a positive outlook and see the best in others. Must demonstrate knowledge of unique challenges to achieving post-graduate success after a liberal arts education. Ability to work nights and weekends as necessary. Ability to travel locally and regionally on a regular basis to meet constituents. Must be able to successfully pass all background checks as applicable to the position Preferred Qualifications : Education: Master's degree in counseling, business or related area of study. Experience with or trained in self-assessment tools such as MBTI, StrengthsFinder, and DiSC. Experience leading peers on programs and/or initiatives. Demonstrated understanding and experience with the Lutheran concept of vocation. Additional Information: Wittenberg is committed to attracting and retaining highly qualified individuals who collectively reflect the diversity of our student body and society at-large.  Please see our notice of nondiscrimination housed on our website. The successful candidate will demonstrate support for diversity, equity and inclusiveness as well as participate in maintaining a respectful, positive work environment. Wittenberg University is committed to preventing and addressing sexual misconduct in our campus community. Click here to view our Title IX policies. Employment at Wittenberg University is contingent upon satisfactory completion of applicable background checks including but not limited to: criminal records, educational verifications, driving records (when job-related), and/or credit history (when job related). For this position, we are unable to sponsor candidates for work visas. Wittenberg University participates in E-Verify to confirm authorization to work in the U.S. Application Instructions: Review of applications will begin immediately and the position will remain open until filled. To apply, please set-up an account in our online recruiting system and upload the following documents in MS Word or Adobe Acrobat format. Resume Cover letter Name, relationship, and contact information of three professional references. Applicants who require accommodation during any stage of the hiring process should contact the Office of Human Resources at (937) 327-7517 or email hure-mail@wittenberg.edu. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Wittenberg University Wittenberg Ave, Springfield, OH 45501-0720"
    },
    "https://wittenberg.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203758": {
      "title": "Director, Center for Personal and Professional Development",
      "description": "Wittenberg University\nJob Posting: Director, Center for Personal and Professional Development Wittenberg University \n\tJob Posting: Director, Center for Personal and Professional Development Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Director, Center for Personal and Professional Development Category: Administrative Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Student Engagement Locations: Springfield, OH Posted: Aug 15, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: 1-84016-50101 Position ID: 203758 Share About Wittenberg University: In surveying the grounds of what is now Wittenberg University, the Rev. Ezra Keller, the college's first president and founder, remarked: \"This is a lovely spot for a literary institution.\" Today, that lovely spot encompasses more than 100 acres of rolling hills and hollows in southwestern Ohio, with architecturally distinctive structures that embrace Wittenberg's past and provide a beautiful backdrop to the teaching excellence and Lutheran-affiliated learning environment that has defined Wittenberg University since its founding in 1845. Nationally recognized for accessible professors, engaging classroom experiences, service opportunities, and valued athletics traditions, Wittenberg is home to 1,200 students, 30 majors, 3 graduate programs, a wealth of pre-professional and cooperative programs, and 25 varsity sports. Wittenberg University is committed to providing a comprehensive and competitive employee benefits package that attracts and retains talent to further the university's mission and contributes to the personal and financial well-being of employees and their families.  From healthcare to our tuition benefit to vacation and holidays, our goal is to help our employees enjoy happy and healthy lifestyles, while maintaining a good work-life balance. Click here to learn more about Wittenberg's employee benefits. Job Description: The Director of the Center for Personal and Professional Development provides strategic leadership, manages staff and budgets, designs and oversees training programs, and ensures alignment of initiatives with institutional priorities, objectives and goals. The Wittenberg Center for Personal and Professional Development (CPPD) is designed to help students grow both personally and professionally. \"Rooted and Open\" calls ELCA universities, rooted in Lutheran theology, to help students explore larger questions about their purpose and calling in life. The center offers structured and informal opportunities for self-reflection, discernment, conversations about vocation and calling, goal setting, and skill-building. This will include individual and group coaching sessions, workshops, guest speakers, identity-building activities, and professional experiential learning opportunities. Duties and Responsibilities include but not limited to: Set the strategic direction for the center, developing and implementing long-term goals, policies, and programs that align with the university's mission and objectives. Monitor day-to-day program delivery, gather assessment, perform data analysis, and recommend improvement to ensure programs meet needs. Provide useful, accurate, and timely data and career outcomes to constituents; Write reports on center success. Collaborate with on-campus partners to enhance programmatic support and offerings for students. Hire, train, supervise, evaluate, and mentor center staff. Financial Management: Prepare annual center budget, authorize purchases, and monitor expenditures. Explore outside-funding initiatives including but not limited to grant funding opportunities and partner sponsorships. Demonstrate support for community and belonging, as well as participate in maintaining a respectful, positive work environment Requirements: Education: Master's degree in counseling, college student personnel, higher education or related area of study. Experience: 3-5 years of progressive experience working in higher education and relevant work experience in career advising or related field Technical Skills: Microsoft Office Must be able to demonstrate the ability to take initiative. Demonstrated experience building relationships with key constituents. Demonstrated ability to solve problems quickly and professionally, anticipate needs, and communicate proactively. Demonstrated success delivering personal and professional development advice. Experience advising on resumes, interviewing and job search strategies. Ability to have a positive outlook and see the best in others. Must demonstrate knowledge of unique challenges to achieving post-graduate success after a liberal arts education. Belief in the fundamental value of a residential, liberal arts education and its application to life after college. Night and weekend work will be required depending on campus events and needs. Open to traveling locally, regionally, and nationally for specific pre-planned programs Must be able to successfully pass all background checks as applicable to the position on campus in Springfield, Ohio, and may be eligible for consideration of a flexible work schedule based on the university's policies which are subject to change. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with or trained in self-assessment tools such as Myers-Briggs Type Indicator, StrengthsFinder, and DiSC assessment. Demonstrated understanding and experience with the Lutheran concept of vocation. Experience working at a small, liberal arts higher education institution. Experience with career services platforms such as Handshake. Additional Information: Wittenberg is committed to attracting and retaining highly qualified individuals who collectively reflect the diversity of our student body and society at-large.  Please see our notice of nondiscrimination housed on our website. The successful candidate will demonstrate support for diversity, equity and inclusiveness as well as participate in maintaining a respectful, positive work environment. Wittenberg University is committed to preventing and addressing sexual misconduct in our campus community. Click here to view our Title IX policies. Employment at Wittenberg University is contingent upon satisfactory completion of applicable background checks including but not limited to: criminal records, educational verifications, driving records (when job-related), and/or credit history (when job related). For this position, we are unable to sponsor candidates for work visas. Wittenberg University participates in E-Verify to confirm authorization to work in the U.S. Application Instructions: Review of applications will begin immediately and the position will remain open until filled. To apply, please set-up an account in our online recruiting system and upload the following documents in MS Word or Adobe Acrobat format. Resume Cover letter Name, relationship, and contact information of three professional references. Applicants who require accommodation during any stage of the hiring process should contact the Office of Human Resources at (937) 327-7517 or email hure-mail@wittenberg.edu. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Wittenberg University Wittenberg Ave, Springfield, OH 45501-0720"
    },
    "https://wittenberg.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=202861": {
      "title": "Student Financial Services Coordinator",
      "description": "Wittenberg University\nJob Posting: Student Financial Services Coordinator Wittenberg University \n\tJob Posting: Student Financial Services Coordinator Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Student Financial Services Coordinator Category: Administrative Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Admission Locations: Springfield, OH Posted: Jul 22, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: 1-84001-50101 Position ID: 202861 Share About Wittenberg University: In surveying the grounds of what is now Wittenberg University, the Rev. Ezra Keller, the college's first president and founder, remarked: \"This is a lovely spot for a literary institution.\" Today, that lovely spot encompasses more than 100 acres of rolling hills and hollows in southwestern Ohio, with architecturally distinctive structures that embrace Wittenberg's past and provide a beautiful backdrop to the teaching excellence and Lutheran-affiliated learning environment that has defined Wittenberg University since its founding in 1845. Nationally recognized for accessible professors, engaging classroom experiences, service opportunities, and valued athletics traditions, Wittenberg is home to 1,500 students, 60 majors, minors and special programs, three graduate programs, and 25 varsity sports. Wittenberg University is committed to providing a comprehensive and competitive employee benefits package that attracts and retains talent to further the university's mission and contributes to the personal and financial well-being of employees and their families.  From healthcare to our tuition benefit to vacation and holidays, our goal is to help our employees enjoy happy and healthy lifestyles, while maintaining a good work-life balance. Click here to learn more about Wittenberg's employee benefits. Job Description: The Student Financial Services Coordinator serves as the primary point of contact for the Office of Student Financial Services, managing front-desk operations for both financial aid and student accounts. This position triages all incoming calls, emails, and walk-in inquiries; supervises student employees staffing the front desk; oversees the indexing of all student and family documents into the office's imaging system (Softdocs); and administers the Ohio State Grant program from eligibility determination through state reporting and reconciliation. This role requires strong customer service skills, sound judgment in routing sensitive inquiries appropriately, and the ability to manage a state grant program with accuracy and attention to compliance detail. Primary Responsibilities include but are not limited to: Front Desk & Customer Service Management Serve as the first point of contact for all Student Financial Services inquiries, triaging calls, emails, and in-person visits to the appropriate financial aid or student accounts staff member. Provide accurate, front-line guidance to students and families on general financial aid and billing questions, escalating complex or sensitive matters as needed. Use conflict resolution skills to de-escalate difficult situations with students or parents while identifying appropriate next steps. Student Employee Supervision Hire, train, schedule, and supervise student employees staffing the front desk. Monitor front desk coverage and workflow to ensure timely response to student and family inquiries. Provide ongoing feedback and coaching to student staff on customer service standards and office procedures. Document Management & Imaging Index all documents received from students and families into the office's Softdocs imaging solution, ensuring accurate categorization and timely processing. Maintain organized, compliant document records in accordance with office retention policies and FERPA requirements. Troubleshoot routine imaging or indexing issues and escalate system problems as needed. Ohio State Grant Program Administration Determine student eligibility for the Ohio State Grant program in accordance with state guidelines. Prepare and submit disbursement rosters to the Ohio Department of Higher Education (or applicable state agency) according to established deadlines. Reconcile Ohio State Grant program activity with the Director of Student Financial Services and the Finance Office, resolving discrepancies as needed. Maintain current knowledge of Ohio State Grant program regulations and reporting requirements, communicating changes to leadership as needed. Requirements: Bachelor's degree, or equivalent combination of education and experience 3-5 years of experience in a customer service, office administration, or higher education setting (financial aid or student accounts experience preferred) Demonstrated supervisory experience or readiness to supervise student staff Strong organizational skills and attention to detail, particularly with document management and compliance-related tasks Excellent phone and email communication skills Preferred Experience with Softdocs or another document imaging system Familiarity with Ohio State Grant program or other state financial aid program administration Technical proficiency with Ellucian Banner and/or Microsoft Office Experience in a front-desk or high-volume customer service role in higher education environment Additional Information: Wittenberg is committed to attracting and retaining highly qualified individuals who collectively reflect the diversity of our student body and society at-large.  Please see our notice of nondiscrimination housed on our website. The successful candidate will demonstrate support for diversity, equity and inclusiveness as well as participate in maintaining a respectful, positive work environment. Wittenberg University is committed to preventing and addressing sexual misconduct in our campus community. Click here to view our Title IX policies. Employment at Wittenberg University is contingent upon satisfactory completion of applicable background checks including but not limited to: criminal records, educational verifications, driving records (when job-related), and/or credit history (when job related). For this position, we are unable to sponsor candidates for work visas. Wittenberg University participates in E-Verify to confirm authorization to work in the U.S. Application Instructions: Review of applications will begin immediately and the position will remain open until filled. To apply, please set-up an account in our online recruiting system and upload the following documents in MS Word or Adobe Acrobat format. 1. Resume 2. Cover letter 3. Name, address, and phone number of three professional references. Applicants who require accommodation during any stage of the hiring process should contact the Office of Human Resources at (937) 327-7517 or email hure-mail@wittenberg.edu. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Wittenberg University Wittenberg Ave, Springfield, OH 45501-0720"
